 privacy fix (checklist item 5, frontend)

Companion to the backend fix removing dealer purchasePrice/profit/
totalExpenses/totalRevenue from partner-facing endpoints - these
fields no longer exist in the API response, so every place these two
pages referenced them (on-screen tables, Excel exports, PDF exports)
needed updating too, or they'd have shown misleading zeros/blanks
instead of the removed data.

partner/cars/page.tsx: removed the Expenses and Profit
columns/display entirely from the on-screen card, the Excel export,
and the PDF export - there's no partner-specific share computed for
this endpoint's car list (only for actual completed sales via
my-earnings), so showing nothing here is more honest than inventing
a number.

partner/earnings/page.tsx: replaced every reference to the old raw
profit field with the new partnerShare figure the backend now
computes (the partner's own earned amount from their agreed revenue
share, not the dealer's raw profit) - relabeled from 'Profit' to
'Your Share' across the on-screen table, Excel export, and PDF
export to accurately describe what the figure actually represents
now. Shows an em dash when no revenue share percentage is set for
that dealer link, rather than a misleading 0.
